# Breaks R-1: a module is the unit of compilation and `import` forms a DAG, so
# the graph has to be acyclic for anything else to hold. A cycle has no
# initialisation order, since a module initialises after every module it
# imports and here each would have to follow the other, and the acyclicity is
# also what makes at most one module able to define any given impl. `dep/loop_a`
# and `dep/loop_b` import each other.
module diagnostics/r1_import_cycle

import dep/loop_a

using dep/loop_a

puts a
